course: dictionary
lesson: 6293
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «The astronauts took their first moonwalk in 1969.» Astronauts and the Moon are the clues, so a moonwalk is a walk on the surface of the Moon.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another sentence. «Jayden did a moonwalk across the dance floor at the disco.» There are no spacecraft here, so a moonwalk must be the famous dance move where you seem to walk forwards but slide backwards.
explain: To check your choice, ask: which meaning fits the clues around the word? Then swap your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is called a multiple-meaning word.
fact: «Moonwalk» can be a noun (a moonwalk) or a verb (to moonwalk).
fact: Meaning 1: a walk on the surface of the Moon by an astronaut, such as Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin on Apollo 11 in 1969.
fact: Meaning 2: a dance move where you seem to walk forwards but slide backwards, made famous by the singer Michael Jackson.
fact: «The Parkes radio telescope in New South Wales helped relay television pictures of the Apollo 11 Moonwalk to the world in 1969.» The clues are Apollo 11, television and the telescope, so here it means the walk on the Moon.
exercise: «The astronauts left their spacecraft for a moonwalk.» What does moonwalk mean here? | A type of boat | *A walk on the surface of the Moon | A quiet stroll home | A dance step at a school disco
exercise: «At the school disco, Ella moonwalked across the stage.» What does moonwalked mean? | Fell asleep on the stage | Walked on the Moon | *Did the backwards-sliding dance move | Ran very fast
exercise: «The Apollo 11 moonwalk was watched by millions on television.» Which word is the clue that tells you the meaning? | Watched | Millions | Television, because it is a machine | *Apollo 11
test: «Neil Armstrong made the first moonwalk in 1969.» Which meaning fits? | A slow walk in the rain | A race around a track | A dance step at a disco | *A walk on the surface of the Moon
test: «Michael Jackson made the moonwalk famous with his dancing.» Which meaning fits? | A rocket launch | A film about astronauts | A walk on the Moon | *A dance move that seems to go forwards but slides backwards
exam: Pick the right meaning for «The children watched the Apollo 11 moonwalk on television.» | *A walk on the surface of the Moon | A dance move at a disco | A walk to school in the rain | A type of spacecraft
